---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import kevinPhoto from '../assets/photos/kevin-at-the-shed.webp';
---
<Base title="Our Story — Windrose Farm" description="Windrose Farm began decades before the land was found — with Aunt Rosie, a compass rose, and a family's long dream of stewardship.">
  <section class="wrap article-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Our Story</p>
    <h1>It began decades before the land</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap article-body prose" style="padding-top: 0;">
    <p>
      Windrose Farm did not begin with the purchase of land. It began decades earlier.
    </p>
    <p>
      One of the earliest inspirations was <strong>Aunt Rosie</strong>, whose lifelong
      commitment to beekeeping, organic gardening, and caring for the land quietly
      demonstrated what true stewardship looked like — long before sustainable
      agriculture became fashionable. Her patience, generosity, and respect for
      nature planted seeds that would eventually grow into Windrose Farm.
    </p>
    <p>
      Years later, after years of dreaming, planning, and searching, we found
      37 acres of windswept Arizona high desert. Many people would have seen an
      empty field. We saw possibility.
    </p>
    <p>
      Windrose Farm is the realization of that vision — a place where family,
      stewardship, craftsmanship, and nature come together.
    </p>
    <figure class="snapshot">
      <Image
        src={kevinPhoto}
        alt="A smiling family member in a sun hat giving a thumbs-up in front of the red machine shed on a bright day"
        widths={[640, 1024, 1600]}
        sizes="(max-width: 72rem) 100vw, 66ch"
      />
      <figcaption>Day one of a project measured in decades. So far, so good.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>
      Our goal is not to create the perfect farm. Our goal is to become better
      stewards every year. Every beehive, every fruit tree, every garden bed,
      every vineyard row, and every building is another chapter in a story we
      hope continues for generations. Some experiments will succeed. Others
      won't. We'll share both — because honest learning is every bit as valuable
      as a successful harvest.
    </p>

    <hr class="rule" style="margin-block: 3rem;" />

    <h2>Why "Windrose"?</h2>
    <p>
      The name draws on the traditional compass rose — guidance, exploration,
      resilience, understanding the natural forces around us. It also reflects
      the property itself, where prevailing winds shape nearly every design
      decision. Rather than forcing the land to conform to us, Windrose Farm
      grows in harmony with nature: following its seasons, respecting its
      limits, embracing its opportunities.
    </p>

    <h2>A vision measured in decades</h2>
    <p>
      This is not a commercial farm or a lifestyle brand. It is first and
      foremost a family legacy project built around stewardship, sustainability,
      lifelong learning, and producing exceptional food through thoughtful,
      organic practices. Over time, Windrose Farm will become:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>A thriving organic apiary</li>
      <li>An organic market garden</li>
      <li>A diverse orchard</li>
      <li>A small vineyard</li>
      <li>Wildlife-friendly habitat</li>
      <li>A demonstration of regenerative agriculture in Arizona's high country</li>
      <li>A gathering place for family and friends</li>
      <li>A legacy to be passed to future generations</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The emphasis is always on building something <em>permanent</em>, not
      something fast.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="dedication">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Dedication</p>
      <h2>For Aunt Rosie</h2>
      <p>
        Windrose Farm is lovingly dedicated to Aunt Rosie. Her lifelong
        commitment to beekeeping, organic gardening, and caring for the land
        helped inspire the vision for this farm. May every blossom visited by
        our bees, every tree planted, every garden tended, and every harvest
        gathered honor the quiet example she set. Her legacy continues to
        bloom at Windrose Farm.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
